• An analysis of macroeconomic conditions and risks LMICs face amid changing global financial and trade conditions and what these shifts imply for these countries’ debt burdens and vulnerabilities;

• A discussion of how rising debt service burdens, elevated financing needs, and changing financing patterns are constraining fiscal space and intensifying debt and rollover risks, as well as the policy priorities for strengthening resilience;

• An analysis of how elevated debt burdens appear to be associated with adverse changes in healthy diet unaffordability in LMICs during periods of global stress and of potential underlying mechanisms, including food import reliance and diversification; and
